WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.686
Reporting completes the workflow by delivering the answer in a form the intended audience can use.

00:00:07.686 --> 00:00:11.420
Start with the requirement and decision context.

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:19.106
The report should make the main finding, confidence, significance, and recommended next step easy to identify.

00:00:19.106 --> 00:00:23.718
An executive summary should be concise without hiding uncertainty.

00:00:23.718 --> 00:00:30.086
Supporting sections can provide a timeline, relationship map, source notes, and analytical rationale.

00:00:30.086 --> 00:00:38.212
Technical readers may need detailed public indicators or infrastructure context, while leaders may need implications and options.

00:00:38.212 --> 00:00:42.384
Cite evidence close to the claim it supports.

00:00:42.384 --> 00:00:46.557
Distinguish confirmed observations, source assertions, and analytical judgments.

00:00:46.557 --> 00:00:52.925
Explain confidence in plain language and use the organization's defined confidence scale consistently.

00:00:52.925 --> 00:00:55.341
Report limitations and gaps.

00:00:55.341 --> 00:01:03.906
Note stale records, ambiguous identities, translation issues, missing primary material, possible source coordination, and areas outside authorized scope.

00:01:03.906 --> 00:01:10.714
Decision-makers need to know what is not established and what could change the conclusion.

00:01:10.714 --> 00:01:15.765
Recommendations should be lawful, proportionate, and tied to the finding.

00:01:15.765 --> 00:01:27.404
They may include internal validation, monitoring an approved public source, correcting exposed information, consulting legal or privacy staff, or collecting a specifically authorized additional record.

00:01:27.404 --> 00:01:31.137
Control dissemination according to sensitivity and purpose.

00:01:31.137 --> 00:01:35.310
Remove irrelevant personal details and avoid unsupported accusations.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:42.557
Capture feedback: did the report answer the question, arrive in time, and support a decision?

00:01:42.557 --> 00:01:48.486
Use that feedback to improve future requirements, collection plans, analysis, and presentation.
